---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import { ShieldCheck, AlertCircle, CheckCircle2, Lock, Heart, Phone, Mail } from 'lucide-astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Child Safeguarding & Protection Policy"
  eyebrow="Zero Tolerance Pledge"
  description="Our sacred commitment and mandatory protocols to ensure the physical, emotional, and psychological safety of every girl we serve."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Safeguarding Policy' }]}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <!-- Safeguarding Commitment Banner -->
    <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/30 mb-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-6">
      <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-secondary-fixed flex items-center justify-center text-secondary flex-shrink-0">
        <ShieldCheck class="w-8 h-8" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="font-label-caps text-secondary font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Unconditional Protection</span>
        <h2 class="font-headline-sm text-primary mt-1">Our Sacred Duty of Care</h2>
        <p class="font-body-sm text-on-surface-variant mt-1 leading-relaxed">
          The Blooming Ones Initiative operates with a zero-tolerance policy regarding child abuse, exploitation, harassment, or negligence. Every staff member, volunteer, and visiting partner is legally and ethically bound by our Safeguarding Charter.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-on-surface leading-relaxed
      [&>p]:text-body-md [&>p]:text-on-surface-variant [&>p]:mb-6 [&>p]:leading-relaxed
      [&>h2]:font-headline-md [&>h2]:text-primary [&>h2]:mt-10 [&>h2]:mb-4
      [&>h3]:font-title-lg [&>h3]:text-primary [&>h3]:mt-6 [&>h3]:mb-3
      [&>ul]:list-disc [&>ul]:pl-6 [&>ul]:mb-6 [&>ul]:space-y-2 [&>ul>li]:text-on-surface-variant
    ">
      <h2>1. Purpose and Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to all trustees, leadership, employees, field volunteers, external photographers, clinical contractors, and visitors participating in activities organized by The Blooming Ones Initiative across schools, community centers, and orphanages in Nigeria.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Core Safeguarding Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Paramount Welfare of the Child:</strong> The rights, best interests, and emotional security of the girl-child take priority over all organizational, operational, or fundraising considerations.</li>
        <li><strong>Equal Dignity and Protection:</strong> Every child has the right to equal protection regardless of socioeconomic background, ethnic origin, religious creed, or disability.</li>
        <li><strong>Two-Adult Rule:</strong> No adult volunteer or team member is ever permitted to be in a closed, isolated room alone with an underage child. All interactions, check-ins, and counseling must occur in open, visible, or co-supervised settings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Recruitment & Volunteer Screening</h2>
      <p>To ensure our spaces remain trusted sanctuaries, every prospective volunteer undergoes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Government-issued identity verification.</li>
        <li>Mandatory reference checks and background inquiries.</li>
        <li>Completion of our Child Safeguarding and Mandatory Reporting Orientation workshop.</li>
        <li>Signing of our formal Code of Conduct before receiving a field deployment pass.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Ethical Photography & Storytelling</h2>
      <p>
        In accordance with our humanitarian ethics, we reject harmful tropes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We obtain informed, signed consent from parents/guardians and schools prior to photographing students.</li>
        <li>Beneficiaries are always photographed respectfully and fully clothed, in empowered posture.</li>
        <li>We never disclose specific residential locations, personal phone numbers, or vulnerable familial details of child beneficiaries.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Confidential Reporting & Whistleblowing Channel</h2>
      <p>
        Any person who observes, suspects, or receives an allegation of child abuse or boundary violation involving our activities is mandated to report immediately to our Designated Safeguarding Officer (DSO).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Confidential Hotline Card -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-8 rounded-3xl bg-primary text-on-primary border border-outline-variant/30 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6 shadow-xl">
      <div>
        <span class="font-label-caps text-secondary-fixed font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Confidential Channel</span>
        <h3 class="font-headline-sm text-on-primary mt-1">Designated Safeguarding Desk</h3>
        <p class="font-body-sm text-surface-dim mt-1 max-w-lg">
          Reports are treated with urgent priority, complete confidentiality, and protected whistleblowing status.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-4 flex-shrink-0">
        <a
          href="mailto:safeguarding@thebloomingones.org"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-surface-bright text-primary font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-surface transition-colors shadow-md"
        >
          <Mail class="w-4 h-4 text-secondary" />
          <span>safeguarding@thebloomingones.org</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
